<title>GERMANY: Bankgesellschaft 9-month operating profit down.</title>
<headline>Bankgesellschaft 9-month operating profit down.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to Sept 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group oper profit after provisions	465  vs     688</p>
<p>    Group risk provisions			 612  vs     542</p>
<p>    Group own-account trading loss	     56  vs	39 profit</p>
<p>    Group net interest income		 2,823  vs   2,531</p>
<p>    Group net commission income		 505  vs     441</p>
<p>    Group admin costs			   2,766  vs   2,420</p>
<p>    Group lending volume		    216,742  vs 200,519</p>
<p>    Group balance sheet total	     315,058  vs 281,553</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German bank is Bankgesellschaft Berlin AG. Results compare with the first nine months of 1995. Analysts' forecasts for operating profit after risk provisions averaged 523.8 million marks and ranged from 506 million marks to 539 million.</p>
<p>Bankgesellschaft had posted an own-account trading loss of 110 million marks after the first six months partly because of writedowns on equity derivatives.</p>
<p>But the bank said the writedowns in the first half had been more than offset by interest income and dividends related to those derivatives.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
